From e752d5801648651cd65abb727ecc63e9080cbea2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dom Cobley <popcornmix@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 09:19:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fbcon: Show fullscreen logo even when quiet

fbcon_init() suppresses the logo when console_loglevel is at or below
CONSOLE_LOGLEVEL_QUIET, so "quiet" (or loglevel<=4) on the command line
stops the fullscreen splash appearing at all. A user who has asked for
fullscreen_logo=1 has explicitly requested a splash, so don't let quiet
override it.

Suggested-by: flyeriNsomniac
Link: https://github.com/raspberrypi/linux/issues/7081
Signed-off-by: Dom Cobley <popcornmix@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/video/fbdev/core/fbcon.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/video/fbdev/core/fbcon.c
+++ b/drivers/video/fbdev/core/fbcon.c
@@ -1055,7 +1055,8 @@ static void fbcon_init(struct vc_data *v
 
 	info = fbcon_info_from_console(vc->vc_num);
 
-	if (logo_shown < 0 && console_loglevel <= CONSOLE_LOGLEVEL_QUIET)
+	if (logo_shown < 0 && console_loglevel <= CONSOLE_LOGLEVEL_QUIET &&
+	    !fullscreen_logo_enabled)
 		logo_shown = FBCON_LOGO_DONTSHOW;
 
 	if (vc != svc || logo_shown == FBCON_LOGO_DONTSHOW ||
